{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ReebChiralitySeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ReebChiralitySeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebChiralityKey_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebChiralityKey_values","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ReebChiralitySeparation.lean#L81-L88","doc":"The five keys are pairwise distinct (the explicit witness list). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebChiralityKey_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebChiralityKey_injective","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ReebChiralitySeparation.lean#L70-L79","doc":"**Reeb level ⊕ chirality SEPARATES the five A₅ irreps** (the composite key\nis injective).  The chirality `±1` breaks the T₂/G Casimir-12 degeneracy\nthat the level alone leaves; all other pairs are already separated by the\nlevel.  This realises the `five_distinct_classes` separation from on-main\ncanonical data, with no geometric angle input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.reebChiralityKey","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.reebChiralityKey","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ReebChiralitySeparation.lean#L67-L68","doc":"The composite key: (Reeb-Casimir level, chirality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebCasimir_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebCasimir_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ReebChiralitySeparation.lean#L59-L65","doc":"**The Reeb level alone does NOT separate the five irreps.**  T₂ and G both\nfirst appear at ℓ = 3, so both have Casimir 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.chirality","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ReebChiralitySeparation.lean#L54-L57","doc":"Chirality of each A₅ irrep: the T₁/T₂ pair (the self-conjugate (3,1,1)\nsplit) carries `±1`; the others are chirality-neutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.reebCasimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.reebCasimir","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ReebChiralitySeparation.lean#L50-L52","doc":"Reeb-spin Casimir at first appearance: `ℓ(ℓ+1)` (classical limit of the\ncontent-Casimir `μ_λ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.firstEll_appears","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.firstEll_appears","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ReebChiralitySeparation.lean#L39-L48","doc":"The `firstEll` value is grounded in `icosBranchingMult`: each irrep's\nmultiplicity entry is nonzero at its `firstEll` (and the table is the\nderived I-character branching).  Entry order is [A, T₁, T₂, G, H]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.firstEll","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.firstEll","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ReebChiralitySeparation.lean#L34-L37","doc":"First angular-momentum level at which each A₅ irrep appears in the SO(3)\ntower, read off `icosBranchingMult` (A@0, T₁@1, H@2, T₂@3, G@3). ","signatureChunk":0}]}